.TH TITANIUM 1
.SH NAME
titanium \- ground-war gun platform game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/titanium
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Titanium
is a port of the TempleOS game of the same name.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
You fly a gun platform up a wrapping 4096-pixel desert battlefield,
over a ground war between 512 enemy and 128 friendly infantry and
tanks who seek each other out and fight hand-to-hand.
The map scrolls at 100 pixels per second while the platform creeps
toward the brown finish line; crossing it, or either side being
wiped out, ends the game.
Holding down the fire key sweeps a stream of bullets; the four
wing-mounted missiles explode with a 100-pixel kill radius that
also levels apartment buildings.
Bullets and missiles do not distinguish friend from foe.
.PP
Scoring follows the original exactly:
+3 for each enemy killed, +5 for each enemy killed by a friendly,
\-100 for each friendly killed by you, \-1 per bullet fired,
\-10 per second of game time, and at game over the surviving
friendlies are counted up at +250 apiece.
The best score is remembered between sessions.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B left / right
Sweep the gun \(+-15 degrees and strafe.
The platform wraps around the screen edges.
.TP
.B space
Fire; hold it down for continuous fire.
.TP
.B z
Fire a left-wing missile.
.TP
.B x
Fire a right-wing missile.
.TP
.B Enter
Restart
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
